# What not to upload to Vercel. The CLI uploads the whole workspace — the web app imports
# `@nap/shared` by source, so `apps/web` alone would not build — and without this that
# includes a gigabyte of `node_modules` and a local `.next`, which exceeds the upload limit.
#
# **Every pattern here is anchored — `/name` for one at the repository root, `**/name` for one
# meant at any depth — and `test/deploy-ignore.ts` fails the build if one is not.** A bare name is
# the recursive form in this syntax, and that is almost never what is meant here: bare `docs`
# excluded `apps/web/src/docs` and `apps/web/src/app/docs` along with the root `docs/`, which
# deleted the `/docs` route on its way to Vercel. Nothing failed. The route and everything it
# imported went missing together, so there was no unresolved import to error on, and the header
# that links to it is not under a `docs/` path and shipped fine — the site built green and served
# a 404 on a page whose own links were live.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo

# The API's business, not the browser's.
/Dockerfile
/.dockerignore
/railway.json
/infra
/test
/docs
